  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nA blocky pattern characterized by a mid level ridge extending from \nthe western Gulf to the western Great Lakes will shift slightly east \ninto the early part of the week. Surface high situated east of the \narea will remain through the weekend. This will offer mainly clear \nskies and light winds which will lead to river valley fog overnight. \n\nA weak surface front will sag south across the area Monday evening into\nthe overnight hours. With a dry airmass - only expect some increase\nin clouds. The front will wash out as another surface high moves \nfrom Ontario to the northeast Atlantic coast. \n\nThe mid level ridge gets slowly suppressed south, breaking down by \nmid week as a short wave lifts out of the southern Plains and up the \nOhio Valley into the Great Lakes.  \n\nThis pattern will offer an extended period of dry conditions which will\npersist well into next week. Temperatures look to be above normal.",
